/-!
# First Betti numbers of five-generated numerical semigroups

Let `S = ⟨n 0 < n 1 < n 2 < n 3 < n 4⟩` be a minimally five-generated numerical semigroup of
width `w = n 4 - n 0`. The toric ideal `I` of `S` over a field `K` is the kernel of
`K[X₀,…,X₄] → K[t]`, `Xᵢ ↦ t ^ (n i)`; its minimal number of generators `μ(I)` is the first
Betti number `β₁` of `K[S]`, stated below as `Submodule.spanRank` (a cardinal).

* `FiveGenBetti.family_spanRank_eq` (Theorem F): for `k ≥ 3`, `q ≥ k − 1`, `m = 2kq + 1`, the
  semigroup `⟨m, m+1, m+k, m+2k−1, m+2k⟩` has `β₁ = 4k + 2` (an explicit minimal presentation
  with `2k+2` ordinary-homogeneous and `2k` inhomogeneous binomials).
* `FiveGenBetti.beta1_five_le_two_width_add_two` (Theorem W, conjectural): `β₁ ≤ 2w + 2` for
  every minimally five-generated `S` with `4 ≤ w ≤ 40`.

Status 2026-10-16: Theorem F is a PROOF_ATTEMPT (docs/PROOF.md), Theorem W a conjecture to be
supported by a certified sweep; version 1 of this development targets F only. The four-generator
case `β₁ ≤ 2w` is Palomar entry PALOMAR-2026-10-07-000005. Proofs are in `Solution.lean`.
-/

/-! ## Proofs (this module)

The definitions of `Challenge.lean` restated verbatim and Theorem F proved by a thin bridge into the
development library (`FiveGenBetti.Family.spanRank_eq`, sorry-free since b0a3671). This module
does not import `Challenge`; the comparator checks that statements and definitions agree. Theorem W
is not restated here (version 1 is family-only; see `Targets/FiniteWidth.lean`). -/

@[expose] public section

namespace FiveGenBetti

/-- The toric ideal of the monoid generated by `n 0, …, n 4`: the kernel of the `K`-algebra map
`K[X₀,…,X₄] → K[t]` sending `X i` to `t ^ n i`. -/
noncomputable def toricIdeal (K : Type*) [Field K] (n : Fin 5 → ℕ) :
    Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 5) K) :=
  RingHom.ker (MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i => (Polynomial.X : Polynomial K) ^ n i)).toRingHom

/-- The generators `m, m+1, m+k, m+2k−1, m+2k` of the extremal family, `m = 2kq + 1`. -/
def familyGens (k q : ℕ) (i : Fin 5) : ℕ :=
  let m := 2 * k * q + 1
  match i.val with
  | 0 => m
  | 1 => m + 1
  | 2 => m + k
  | 3 => m + (2 * k - 1)
  | _ => m + 2 * k

/-- `n` minimally generates its monoid: no `n i` lies in the submonoid generated by the others. -/
def MinimallyGenerates (n : Fin 5 → ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ i : Fin 5, n i ∉ AddSubmonoid.closure (n '' {j | j ≠ i})

/-- **Theorem F.** The extremal family attains `β₁ = 4k + 2`. -/
theorem family_spanRank_eq (K : Type*) [Field K] (k q : ℕ) (hk : 3 ≤ k) (hq : k - 1 ≤ q) :
    (toricIdeal K (familyGens k q)).spanRank = (4 * k + 2 : ℕ) := by
  exact Family.spanRank_eq K k q hk hq

end FiveGenBetti
